駆け抜ける世界
we run through this world.

36
00:06:40,888 --> 00:06:44,288
I pray among the stars...

37
00:06:44,288 --> 00:06:47,288
わたしはいつも祈ってる
I am always praying.

38
00:06:47,288 --> 00:06:50,088
熱い想いをぶつけたら
If I pour out my passionate feelings,

39
00:06:50,088 --> 00:06:55,588
奇跡さえ起こせるから
I can even make miracles happen!

40
00:07:07,588 --> 00:07:10,588
この景色すべては
This entire scenery

41
00:07:10,588 --> 00:07:13,588
淋しさで出来てる
is made of loneliness.

42
00:07:13,588 --> 00:07:19,088
願うだけで すぐにそばにいられた
Just by wishing, I could be by your side right away.

43
00:07:20,588 --> 00:07:23,588
あの頃の姿を
The shape of those days...

44
00:07:23,588 --> 00:07:26,588
追い求めさまよう
wandering in search of it.

45
00:07:26,588 --> 00:07:32,088
きっと火花、言葉、ここにあるから
Surely because the spark and words are here.

46
00:07:33,888 --> 00:07:35,888
EXE! 懐かしい歌声
EXE! A nostalgic singing voice...

47
00:07:37,088 --> 00:07:39,588
EXE! 今聞こえる
EXE! I can hear it now!

48
00:07:40,588 --> 00:07:48,088
EXE! 真空の中でも受け取れるのはなぜ
EXE! Why can I receive it even in a vacuum?

49
00:07:50,088 --> 00:07:54,088
「通」じあうこのよろこびを感じたい
I want to feel this joy of connecting with you,

50
00:07:54,088 --> 00:07:59,088
場所も時間も飛び越えて
leaping across time and space,

51
00:07:59,088 --> 00:08:03,588
分け合える世代
in a generation sharing with each other.

52
00:08:03,588 --> 00:08:07,288
「信」じあうことがすべてと悟ったよ
I've realized that believing in each other is everything.

53
00:08:07,288 --> 00:08:10,288
君をもう一度見つけたら
Once I find you again,

54
00:08:10,288 --> 00:08:16,588
涙さえ輝くから
even my tears will shine!

55
00:08:47,088 --> 00:08:49,088
幾千の

56
00:08:49,088 --> 00:08:51,088
儚い鼓動 惜しみなく
...fleeting heartbeats, without regret...

57
00:08:51,088 --> 00:08:54,588
流れる時を追い越して
speeding past the flowing time,

58
00:08:54,588 --> 00:08:59,588
駆け抜ける世界
we run through this world.

59
00:08:59,588 --> 00:09:05,588
「通」じ合うこのよろこびを感じたい
I want to feel this joy of connecting with you,

60
00:09:05,588 --> 00:09:10,288
場所も時間も飛び越えて
leaping across time and space,

61
00:09:10,288 --> 00:09:12,588
分け合える世代
in a generation sharing with each other.

62
00:09:12,588 --> 00:09:16,288
「信」じあうことが全てと悟ったよ
I've realized that believing in each other is everything.

63
00:09:16,288 --> 00:09:19,288
君をもう一度みつけたら
Once I find you again,

64
00:09:19,288 --> 00:09:26,088
涙さえ輝くから
even my tears will shine!

65
00:09:49,088 --> 00:09:53,388
もうこの世界には、人はあまり残っていない
There aren't many people left in this world anymore.

66
00:09:53,588 --> 00:10:01,088
文明が崩壊して、インフラも何もかもなくなってしまったのだから、仕方ないことだと思う
Civilization collapsed, and all infrastructure was lost, so I guess it can't be helped.

67
00:10:01,288 --> 00:10:03,088
だけど旅をしていると、何か...
But as I travel, something...

68
00:10:03,409 --> 00:10:09,409
旅をしていると、何かに引き寄せられるように誰かと出会うことがある。
When you are traveling, you sometimes meet someone as if drawn to them by something.

69
00:10:10,209 --> 00:10:11,909
こんな風に。
Just like this.

70
00:10:12,909 --> 00:10:13,909
こんにちは。
Hello there.

71
00:10:13,909 --> 00:10:16,209
こんにちは。あなたは？
Hello. And you are?

72
00:10:16,909 --> 00:10:20,909
私はAZKi。この世界の地図を作りながら
I am AZKi. While drawing a map of this world,

73
00:10:20,909 --> 00:10:25,909
色々なところを調査する「開拓者」をしてるわ。キミは？
I work as a pioneer, surveying various places. What about you?

74
00:10:26,609 --> 00:10:28,909
あたしは旅をしてるんだ。
I am on a journey.

75
00:10:28,909 --> 00:10:33,409
なくなってしまった大切なものを探すために。
To search for something precious that was lost.

76
00:10:33,909 --> 00:10:35,909
大切なもの？
Something precious?

77
00:10:36,209 --> 00:10:39,909
うん。音楽を。
Yes... music.

78
00:10:40,409 --> 00:10:45,909
ふーん。そう、この世界線ではそうなのね。
I see. So in this worldline, that's how it is.

79
00:10:46,409 --> 00:10:48,909
でもあなたは覚えているはずだわ。
But I'm sure you still remember.

80
00:10:49,209 --> 00:10:50,209
ん？
Huh?

81
00:10:50,409 --> 00:10:53,409
記憶にはなくても、
Even if it's not in your memory,

82
00:10:53,409 --> 00:10:56,409
胸の奥の深いところに、いっしょに過ごした時間……
deep down in your heart, the times we spent together...

83
00:10:57,409 --> 00:10:59,909
気持ちを一つにした瞬間を。
The moment our feelings became one.

84
00:11:00,409 --> 00:11:06,909
だってあなたにとってそれは……とても大事なものだったはずだから。
Because to you, that should have been... something very important.

85
00:11:30,509 --> 00:11:31,509
あぁ
Ah...

86
00:11:31,509 --> 00:11:33,909
君が好きな服
The clothes you like

87
00:11:33,909 --> 00:11:37,209
濡れたままだね保存
are still wet, aren't they?

88
00:11:37,209 --> 00:11:40,409
こんな夜だから
Because on a night like this,

89
00:11:40,409 --> 00:11:43,909
響かせてミュージック
make the music echo.

90
00:11:43,909 --> 00:11:47,609
お気に入りの歌は
Your favorite song,

91
00:11:47,609 --> 00:11:51,409
君は知らない
you don't know it.

92
00:11:51,409 --> 00:11:54,609
君だけ知らない
Only you don't know it.

93
00:11:59,209 --> 00:12:02,909
感情論を　君にだけぶつけて
Throwing my emotional arguments only at you,

94
00:12:02,909 --> 00:12:06,609
傷ついたフリしてるけど<
I pretend to be hurt, but...

95
00:12:06,609 --> 00:12:10,409
完全な嘘　いつも言いたいくらい
It's a complete lie, so much that I always want to say it.

96
00:12:10,409 --> 00:12:13,909
もっと確かめてみる
I'll try to make sure even more.

97
00:12:13,909 --> 00:12:17,609
ナンセンス？　だけど涙出る
Nonsense? But the tears still flow.

98
00:12:17,609 --> 00:12:20,409
見ないでよ　ひどい顔なの
Don't look, I look awful.

99
00:12:20,409 --> 00:12:23,909
単純だって言われたくないよ
I don't want to be called simple.

100
00:12:23,909 --> 00:12:27,409
もっと確かめてみて
Try to make sure even more.

101
00:12:41,609 --> 00:12:42,909
ねぇ
Hey...

102
00:12:42,909 --> 00:12:45,209
朝が来る前に
Before morning comes,

103
00:12:45,209 --> 00:12:48,409
連れ出しててみ
try taking me out.

104
00:12:48,409 --> 00:12:51,909
こんな夜だから
Because on a night like this,

105
00:12:51,909 --> 00:12:55,209
鳴り止まないミュージック
the music won't stop ringing.

106
00:12:55,209 --> 00:12:58,909
お気に入りの曲は
Your favorite song,

107
00:12:58,909 --> 00:13:02,909
君は踊らない
you won't dance to it.

108
00:13:02,909 --> 00:13:06,909
君だけ踊らない
Only you won't dance.

109
00:13:10,609 --> 00:13:14,209
感情論で　君を傷つけて
Hurting you with emotional arguments,

110
00:13:14,209 --> 00:13:17,909
こんな人　嫌になるでしょ？
You must be getting sick of someone like me, right?

111
00:13:17,909 --> 00:13:21,609
純情なんて　呆れるくらいに
Pure heart? To an amazing degree,

112
00:13:21,609 --> 00:13:25,209
ホント似合わないけど
it really doesn't suit me, but...

113
00:13:25,209 --> 00:13:28,609
テンションちょっと上げて知らんぷり
Raising my spirits a bit and pretending not to care,

114
00:13:28,609 --> 00:13:32,209
困らせたい　そんな気分よ
I want to trouble you, that's just how I feel.

115
00:13:32,209 --> 00:13:35,909
単純だって言われたくないよ
I don't want to be called simple.

116
00:13:35,909 --> 00:13:39,209
きっと我が儘だけど
I'm surely selfish, but...

117
00:13:39,209 --> 00:13:40,609
完全少女論
Complete Girl Theory,

118
00:13:40,609 --> 00:13:42,209
自己中心論
Egocentrism Theory,

119
00:13:42,209 --> 00:13:43,609
気分上々論
Feeling Great Theory,

120
00:13:43,609 --> 00:13:45,209
そういいんじゃない？
Isn't that fine?

121
00:13:45,209 --> 00:13:46,909
感情暴走論
Emotion Runaway Theory,

122
00:13:46,909 --> 00:13:48,409
リカバリ不可能論
Irrecoverable Theory,

123
00:13:48,409 --> 00:13:52,209
一苦労でしょ？
It's a lot of trouble, isn't it?

124
00:13:52,409 --> 00:13:56,209
ほんのちょっと手を伸ばして
Just stretch your hand out a little bit.

125
00:13:56,209 --> 00:13:59,909
きっと全然気づかない
You surely won't notice at all.

126
00:13:59,909 --> 00:14:03,609
笑い合うよ　朝が来たら
We'll laugh together when morning comes.

127
00:14:03,609 --> 00:14:07,609
大丈夫だから
Because it'll be alright.

128
00:14:07,909 --> 00:14:11,909
感情論を　君に投げつけて
Hurting you with emotional arguments,

129
00:14:11,909 --> 00:14:15,609
演じてるフリしてるけど
I pretend to be acting, but...

130
00:14:15,609 --> 00:14:19,409
完全そうそう　いつも言いたいくらい
Completely, yes, so much that I always want to say it.

131
00:14:19,409 --> 00:14:22,409
君は優しすぎるけど
You are way too kind, but...

132
00:14:22,409 --> 00:14:26,209
感情論も　君に投げつけて
Hurling emotional arguments at you too,

133
00:14:26,209 --> 00:14:29,609
傷ついたフリしてるけど
I pretend to be hurt, but...

134
00:14:29,609 --> 00:14:33,409
完全そうそう　いつも言いたいくらい
Completely, yes, so much that I always want to say it.

135
00:14:33,409 --> 00:14:37,209
もっと確かめてみる
I'll try to make sure even more.

136
00:15:01,087 --> 00:15:02,587
(……)
(......)

137
00:15:02,887 --> 00:15:05,887
(さっきのは……なんだったんだろう)
(What was that... just now?)

138
00:15:06,187 --> 00:15:10,087
(たくさんの人たちと、)
(Surrounded by so many people...)

139
00:15:10,087 --> 00:15:14,387
(その人たちが発する熱気に包まれて、あたしはすごくワクワクしてた)
(...and wrapped in their excitement, I was so thrilled.)

140
00:15:15,187 --> 00:15:18,987
(なんだかすごく懐かしい感じがした……)
(It felt somehow so nostalgic...)

141
00:15:20,587 --> 00:15:23,587
"ねえねえ、キミ、大丈夫？"
"Hey, are you okay?"

142
00:15:24,087 --> 00:15:24,787
"え？"
"Eh?"

143
00:15:25,087 --> 00:15:28,087
"なんか顔色がよくなかったからさ。"
"You didn't look very well."

144
00:15:28,087 --> 00:15:31,587
"あ、うちはミオだよ。占い師をやってる。"
"Oh, I'm Mio. I'm a fortune teller."

145
00:15:32,087 --> 00:15:36,587
"お、キミ、何かを探してるね。そう占いにでてる。"
"Oh, you're looking for something. That's what my fortune says."

146
00:15:37,087 --> 00:15:38,287
"わかるの？"
"You can tell?"

147
00:15:38,587 --> 00:15:40,887
"うん。よかったら話してみて。"
"Yeah. If you'd like, try talking to me."

148
00:15:40,887 --> 00:15:43,587
"何か力になれるかもしれないし。"
"Maybe I can be of help."

149
00:15:44,087 --> 00:15:45,587
"実は――"
"Actually—"

150
00:15:47,887 --> 00:15:52,587
"なるほど――キミは「オンガク」を探してるんだね。"
"I see... So you're looking for \"music.\""

151
00:15:53,087 --> 00:15:56,587
"それなら、あそこに行ってみればいいんじゃない？"
"In that case, why don't you try going there?"

152
00:15:57,087 --> 00:16:00,887
"世界の果てにあるっていう、光の塔。"
"The Tower of Light, which is said to be at the end of the world."

153
00:16:01,087 --> 00:16:06,087
"そこには「天使」が住んでて、やって来た人の願いを叶えてくれるんだって。"
"An \"angel\" lives there, and she grants the wishes of those who visit."

154
00:16:06,387 --> 00:16:11,587
"だからそこに行ってお願いをすれば、キミの探しものも見つかるんじゃないかな。"
"So if you go there and make a wish, maybe you'll find what you're looking for."

155
00:16:12,087 --> 00:16:15,587
"親切にありがとう。そこに行ってみることにするよ！"
"Thanks for your kindness. I'll decide to go there!"

156
00:16:16,087 --> 00:16:19,587
"どういたしまして。でもお礼なんていらないって。"
"You're welcome. But I told you, no thanks are necessary."

157
00:16:20,087 --> 00:16:21,087
"？"
"?"

158
00:16:21,587 --> 00:16:25,587
"だってうちは――キミのことが大好きだから！"
"Because I... really love you!"

159
00:16:25,587 --> 00:16:28,587
"ずっとずっと前からね！"
"From way, way back!"

160
00:16:40,087 --> 00:16:45,087
[曲名] コトダマ紡ぐ未来 / 作詞：石川泰 作曲：田辺トシノ
"[Song] Kotodama Tsumugu Mirai / Lyrics: Yasushi Ishikawa, Composition: Toshino Tanabe"

161
00:17:01,887 --> 00:17:07,087
遥か 遠く
Far... in the distance...

162
00:17:07,587 --> 00:17:14,387
続く 果てなき道
...this endless road continues on.

163
00:17:14,587 --> 00:17:19,887
それでも いつか
Even so, someday...

164
00:17:19,887 --> 00:17:26,587
たどり着くと信じて
...believing that I will reach it.

165
00:17:26,587 --> 00:17:32,387
たとえ 今は
Even if, for now...

166
00:17:32,587 --> 00:17:39,087
辛く 厳しくても
...it is painful and harsh,

167
00:17:39,087 --> 00:17:44,387
小さな 笑顔
...a tiny smile...

168
00:17:44,387 --> 00:17:51,587
守る 全て捧げて
...I will protect it, giving my everything.

169
00:17:51,587 --> 00:17:56,587
心 重なる
Our hearts overlap...

170
00:17:57,087 --> 00:18:04,287
言葉より強い絆に
...into a bond stronger than words.

171
00:18:04,287 --> 00:18:09,587
染め上げてゆく
We will color ourselves...

172
00:18:09,587 --> 00:18:16,087
一つになるコトバで
...with the word that makes us one.

173
00:18:19,587 --> 00:18:25,087
記憶たどる 追憶の旅
Tracing back memories, a journey of recollection...

174
00:18:25,587 --> 00:18:31,087
続けて
...continues.

175
00:18:31,587 --> 00:18:37,087
あらゆることを 受け止めるから
Since I will accept everything...

176
00:18:37,087 --> 00:18:42,587
言葉はいらないの
...no words are needed anymore.

177
00:18:43,087 --> 00:18:51,087
それは永遠に
That is for eternity.

178
00:19:01,587 --> 00:19:07,087
いつも 近く
Always close...

179
00:19:07,587 --> 00:19:14,087
そばで見つめていたけど保存
...I was watching over you from your side, but...

180
00:19:14,387 --> 00:19:19,587
気づかず いても
...even if you didn't notice...

181
00:19:19,887 --> 00:19:26,587
今は 遠く感じる
...now I feel so far away.

182
00:19:27,087 --> 00:19:32,587
あとを 追いかけ
Chasing after you...

183
00:19:33,087 --> 00:19:38,887
絆から愛に変われば"
...if our bond turns into love,

184
00:19:39,087 --> 00:19:44,587
染め上げてゆく
We will color ourselves completely...

185
00:19:44,587 --> 00:19:51,587
二人だけの秘密"
...with a secret meant only for the two of us.

186
00:19:54,087 --> 00:20:00,087
思いを込めた 言葉の強さ
The strength of words infused with feelings...

187
00:20:00,087 --> 00:20:03,087
信じ
...believing in them...

188
00:20:03,102 --> 00:20:06,302
...信じてる
...believing.

189
00:20:06,902 --> 00:20:12,602
口にした時 覚悟していた
When I spoke it, I was prepared.

190
00:20:12,702 --> 00:20:18,102
未来を紡ぐために
In order to spin the future.

191
00:20:43,302 --> 00:20:46,402
気がつけばほら
Before I knew it, look...

192
00:20:46,602 --> 00:20:50,602
心に宿る
...lodged in my heart,

193
00:20:50,902 --> 00:20:55,602
ともしび
...is a light.

194
00:20:56,102 --> 00:20:58,602
小さな光
If our tiny lights...

195
00:20:58,802 --> 00:21:01,602
寄り添い合えば
...draw close together,

196
00:21:01,902 --> 00:21:07,602
その未来を指して
...they will point to that future.

197
00:21:08,302 --> 00:21:10,902
青く広がる
Spreading out in blue,

198
00:21:10,902 --> 00:21:14,302
晴れ渡る空
is the clear sky.

199
00:21:15,602 --> 00:21:19,902
見上げる
We look up at it.

200
00:21:20,602 --> 00:21:22,902
もう言葉すら
Because we no longer

201
00:21:22,902 --> 00:21:26,102
いらないから
even need words,

202
00:21:26,602 --> 00:21:32,602
ただ 抱きしめていた
just hold each other tight.

203
00:21:32,902 --> 00:21:39,102
時は 永遠に
Time will go on forever.

204
00:22:07,302 --> 00:22:11,902
（降り注ぐ 雨のような歓声）
(Cheers raining down like rain.)

205
00:22:11,902 --> 00:22:19,602
（その中で、きらびやかな服を着たあたしは、幸せそうな笑顔で手を振っている）
(Among them, dressed in brilliant clothes, I wave with a happy smile.)

206
00:22:19,602 --> 00:22:24,602
（まるで、もう一人のあたしのように）
(Just like another me.)

207
00:22:25,602 --> 00:22:30,102
（世界の果てにあるという光の塔）
(The Tower of Light, said to be at the end of the world.)

208
00:22:30,302 --> 00:22:35,302
（「オンガク」を探すために、あたしはそこを目指すことに決めた）
(To find "Music," I decided to head there.)

209
00:22:35,602 --> 00:22:42,602
（何日かかるかわからないけど、幸いなことに時間はたくさんある）
(I don't know how many days it will take, but fortunately, I have plenty of time.)

210
00:22:42,602 --> 00:22:44,902
（ただ……）
(But...)

211
00:22:44,902 --> 00:22:48,602
お腹、空いた……
I'm hungry...

212
00:22:50,402 --> 00:22:54,602
なんでわためを見てお腹を鳴らしてるの！？
Why is your stomach growling while looking at Watame?!

213
00:22:54,602 --> 00:22:59,602
え、わからないけど、何かキミを見たら急に
Eh, I don't know, but looking at you just suddenly made me...

214
00:22:59,602 --> 00:23:02,102
わためは非常食じゃないよー！
Watame is not emergency food!

215
00:23:02,102 --> 00:23:06,602
見逃してくれたら、代わりにわためが歌うから～
If you spare me, Watame will sing instead!

216
00:23:07,102 --> 00:23:10,602
……ウタ？
...Sing?

217
00:23:10,602 --> 00:23:13,602
ウタって……なに？
What is... singing?

218
00:23:13,602 --> 00:23:17,102
え、キミ、歌を知らないの？
Eh? You don't know what singing is?

219
00:23:17,102 --> 00:23:23,602
よーし、じゃあ、わためが教えてあげるよ、歌っていうのはね～
Alright! Then Watame will teach you. Singing is...

220
00:23:35,502 --> 00:23:38,402
滅びていくこのステラ
This stella is perishing,

221
00:23:38,402 --> 00:23:40,902
絆を辿るストーリー
A story tracing our bonds.

222
00:23:40,902 --> 00:23:43,102
受け継ぐ想いが
May the thoughts passed down

223
00:23:43,102 --> 00:23:47,102
生まれ変われますように
be reborn anew.

224
00:23:49,102 --> 00:23:54,102
breath of stella
[Title: breath of stella]

225
00:23:57,602 --> 00:23:59,902
目の前
Before me,

226
00:23:59,902 --> 00:24:03,102
現れた無表情は
an expressionless face appeared.

227
00:24:03,102 --> 00:24:05,902
誰にも
Showing affection

228
00:24:05,902 --> 00:24:08,602
懐を見せないまま
to no one.

229
00:24:08,602 --> 00:24:11,602
事象が
Phenomena

230
00:24:11,602 --> 00:24:14,102
世界を歪ませて
distorted the world,

231
00:24:14,102 --> 00:24:16,702
光が
And the light

232
00:24:16,702 --> 00:24:19,602
ただ眩しすぎた
was simply too dazzling.

233
00:24:19,902 --> 00:24:22,502
燦々と照りつける
Scorching brilliantly,

234
00:24:22,502 --> 00:24:25,102
荒野に残した足跡
the footprints left in the wasteland.

235
00:24:25,102 --> 00:24:27,502
与えられたのなら
If it was given to me,

236
00:24:27,502 --> 00:24:30,102
守るものだけ
only what must be protected.

237
00:24:30,202 --> 00:24:33,102
滅びていくこのステラ
This stella is perishing,

238
00:24:33,102 --> 00:24:35,502
叶うことがないとしても
even if it will never come true.

239
00:24:35,502 --> 00:24:37,102
変えよう
Let's change

240
00:24:37,102 --> 00:24:38,102
世界を
the world,

241
00:24:38,102 --> 00:24:40,502
灯していく
lighting the way.

242
00:24:40,502 --> 00:24:43,702
震える手が弾いた
A trembling hand pulled back

243
00:24:43,702 --> 00:24:46,302
意味を持たない銃口
the meaningless muzzle of a gun.

244
00:24:46,302 --> 00:24:48,102
輝く
Beneath

245
00:24:48,102 --> 00:24:49,502
星の下
the shining stars,

246
00:24:49,502 --> 00:24:52,902
わたしは今息をする
I am breathing right now.

247
00:24:57,702 --> 00:25:00,302
それなら
If so,

248
00:25:00,302 --> 00:25:03,102
あなたは騙したんだ
you deceived me.

249
00:25:03,094 --> 00:25:05,194
今なら
If it's now...

250
00:25:05,194 --> 00:25:08,894
全て分かってしまう
I understand everything...

251
00:25:08,894 --> 00:25:11,594
名前を
Even if you

252
00:25:11,594 --> 00:25:14,494
呼んでくれていても
were calling my name,

253
00:25:14,494 --> 00:25:17,094
私に
it was not

254
00:25:17,094 --> 00:25:19,894
向けられていなかった
directed at me.

255
00:25:19,894 --> 00:25:22,094
消える日の前でただ
Just standing still before the day of disappearance,

256
00:25:22,094 --> 00:25:25,094
立ち尽くして煙る灰
the smoldering ashes.

257
00:25:25,094 --> 00:25:27,094
命の理屈が今
The logic of life now

258
00:25:27,094 --> 00:25:30,194
答えを迫る
demands an answer.

259
00:25:30,194 --> 00:25:32,894
滅びていくその中で
Within that decaying world,

260
00:25:32,894 --> 00:25:35,494
息を切らしたバトルクライ保存
a breathless battle cry.

261
00:25:35,494 --> 00:25:38,394
崩れた絆を保存
Shaking off

262
00:25:38,394 --> 00:25:41,294
振りほどいて
the shattered bonds,

263
00:25:41,294 --> 00:25:43,894
お願いどうかそばにいて
please, somehow stay by my side.

264
00:25:43,894 --> 00:25:46,694
声が重星に求めた
My voice pleaded to the binary stars.

265
00:25:46,694 --> 00:25:49,094
終わりと始まりの
Within the time of the end

266
00:25:49,094 --> 00:25:52,094
時のなかで
and the beginning...

267
00:25:52,094 --> 00:25:56,094
ああ
Ah...

268
00:26:03,094 --> 00:26:08,094
瞳の奥に澄んだ
Clear in the depths of your eyes...

269
00:26:08,094 --> 00:26:13,894
壊れかけている心の荷物
the baggage of a heart on the verge of breaking.

270
00:26:13,894 --> 00:26:18,594
引き金にかけた指
The finger placed on the trigger...

271
00:26:18,594 --> 00:26:24,094
先が示す未来を祈るだろう
will probably pray for the future it points to.

272
00:26:26,594 --> 00:26:30,094
滅びてゆくこのステラ
This Stella that is decaying,

273
00:26:30,094 --> 00:26:32,594
瞬きの数の傷
scars as numerous as the blinks of an eye.

274
00:26:32,594 --> 00:26:37,594
心がこのまま途絶えてしまっても
Even if my heart ceases like this,

275
00:26:37,594 --> 00:26:40,594
私の生まれた理由も保存
the reason for my birth,

276
00:26:40,594 --> 00:26:43,594
手放さないでお願い
please don't let it go.

277
00:26:43,594 --> 00:26:46,094
終わりと始まりの
Within the time of the end

278
00:26:46,094 --> 00:26:48,094
時のなかで
and the beginning...

279
00:26:48,094 --> 00:26:54,594
ああ
Ah...

280
00:26:57,094 --> 00:26:59,594
私はここにいるよ
I am right here.

281
00:26:59,594 --> 00:27:02,094
何度も確かめられるよ
We can confirm it as many times as it takes.

282
00:27:02,094 --> 00:27:05,594
そう、心の存在と名前を
Yes, the existence and name of the heart.

283
00:27:05,594 --> 00:27:08,094
あなたが生き抜いた世界は
The world you survived

284
00:27:08,094 --> 00:27:11,094
まだ私の中で息をする
still breathes inside of me.

285
00:27:34,094 --> 00:27:40,094
（光、光、光）
(Light, light, light...)

286
00:27:40,094 --> 00:27:47,094
（その星のようなきらめきが――頭に焼きついて離れない）
(That star-like brilliance is burned into my mind and won't leave.)

287
00:27:48,094 --> 00:27:53,094
（あの子がやっていたことはなんだったんだろう？）
(What was it that she was doing?)

288
00:27:53,094 --> 00:28:00,094
（「ウタ」だって言ってたけど……初めて聞く言葉だ）
(She called it a "song," but... it's a word I've heard for the first time.)

289
00:28:00,094 --> 00:28:07,094
（だけど「ウタ」は、あたしの心の深いところに確かに染み込んできた……）
(But that "song" definitely soaked deep into my heart...)

290
00:28:10,094 --> 00:28:13,094
静かだなー……
"It's so quiet..."

291
00:28:13,094 --> 00:28:19,094
（この世界は、ずっと静寂に包まれている）
(This world is always wrapped in silence.)

292
00:28:19,094 --> 00:28:27,094
（だけどさっきのあれは――「ウタ」は、そのどれとも違った）
(But that thing from earlier—that "song"—was different from any of that.)

293
00:28:27,094 --> 00:28:31,094
（あれは、なんだったんだろう……）
(What was that, I wonder...)

294
00:28:31,094 --> 00:28:40,094
（あと別れ際にくれたこの頭につける道具は……？ 遺物……？）
(And what is this tool for my head that she gave me when we parted...? A relic...?)

295
00:28:41,094 --> 00:28:46,094
（確か「ヘッドセット」って言ってた）
(I think she called it a "headset.")

296
00:28:46,094 --> 00:28:52,094
